# Both of these are PUBLIC values, baked into a static bundle that anyone can
# download. That is fine — they are meant to be public.
#
# What must never appear here, or anywhere in webapp/, is the Supabase SERVICE
# key. It bypasses RLS entirely; this app's whole security model is that it
# talks to Postgres as `authenticated` and the policies decide what comes back.
# `npm run verify:build` greps the built output to enforce that.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
